Take dec:edge-orthogonality forward, and remove a temp file I committed by mistake

TWO THINGS, one of them cleanup of my own litter.

① req:a-vocabulary-distinction-proves-it-is-read (proposed)

Anthony: "agree on taking forward dec:edge-orthogonality."

That decision is ACCEPTED and states the principle — a vocabulary distinction
earns its keep only if a computation reads it. It was applied ONCE, by hand,
retiring VALIDATES and ENABLES on exactly that reasoning, and nothing has
computed it since. The principle has been true and unenforced ever since.

The measurement that made the case, run against reflow2's own 1,873-node design:
EIGHT of sixty edge types are declared and unreached on every test (not
instantiated, not in the propagation table, never named in non-test Rust) —
COMPLIES_WITH, CONTAINS_EPOCH, EVOLVES_INTO, IMPOSES, MITIGATES, SUPERSEDES,
SUPPLEMENTS, VIOLATES_RULE. Seven of twenty-nine node types have zero instances.
Five more edges are instantiated but reached only generically.

THREE HAD COMPLAINTS FILED BY dev_storyflow HOURS EARLIER, which is what makes
it a class rather than tidiness: VIOLATES_RULE undiscoverable through
describe_schema for the pair its name describes; QualityGate "I could not find
an honest use"; Anchor already open as its own decision.

WHY IT NEVER SURFACED: every detector is instance-level and this is a
vocabulary-level fact. A declared type with zero instances produces nothing for
any detector to anchor on, so the accumulation is invisible by construction.

⚠️ TWO BOUNDS WRITTEN INTO THE REQUIREMENT RATHER THAN LEFT TO BE FOUND. It must
not fire on a CONSUMER'S design for not using reflow2's whole vocabulary — a
demonstrator legitimately has empty node types, and nagging correct work is the
failure the phase-nudge doctrine exists to prevent; the defensible subject is
reflow2's own shipped vocabulary. And whatever is built must be READ by
something, or it becomes a ninth unreached thing — which has already happened to
`enforced` and to both retirement edges.

MECHANISM DELIBERATELY LEFT OPEN. dec:idea-detect-vocabulary-that-nothing-reaches
holds four shapes with their counters. Anthony agreed the principle should be
carried forward; he has not chosen the shape, and dec:certainty-derived forbids
recording that on his behalf.

② Remove msg.tmp.txt

A scratch commit-message file I wrote during an amend and then committed to main
in #127. Third consequence of that one botched sequence: the same amend also
truncated #127's commit subject, and the shell-quoting attempt before it mangled
a PR body. Deleted here rather than left as litter.

